1
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:30,390
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:06,220
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION.

3
00:02:09,950 --> 00:02:12,790
Soldiers! Arrest Osman!

4
00:02:13,130 --> 00:02:14,910
Alişar Bey!

5
00:02:15,870 --> 00:02:19,090
How could you take a Bey's
son from a Bey's Tent?

6
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:25,090
You are standing in
front of a banner lord.

7
00:02:25,510 --> 00:02:27,950
Sheathe that dagger.

8
00:02:28,850 --> 00:02:31,100
You put down your blades too.

9
00:02:35,090 --> 00:02:38,430
I will bathe this Tent with the
blood of your soldiers, Alişar Bey!

10
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:40,910
Get away from my brother!

11
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:43,040
Stand back, Gürbüz!

12
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:45,570
Don't make me hurt you too!

13
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:55,540
How did you find out
Kalonoz was dead, Alişar Bey?

14
00:02:58,350 --> 00:02:59,580
I was in the castle.

15
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:04,760
They told me the killers
of Kalonoz were the Kayıs.

16
00:03:04,790 --> 00:03:08,410
Dündar Bey, who are they to
talk while you stand there?

17
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,240
We...

18
00:03:19,370 --> 00:03:21,790
... are the Kayı, Alişar Bey.

19
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:29,600
We know no will than Allah's and
no chairmanship than His messenger's.

20
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:37,730
Dündar Bey...

21
00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:39,800
... think thoroughly.

22
00:03:41,330 --> 00:03:46,370
This ends either by
mass execution or by exile.

23
00:03:49,290 --> 00:03:52,930
Wouldn't the Mongol you are
loyal to ask you about this?

24
00:03:57,050 --> 00:04:01,050
We say Osman is innocent,
don't you understand?

25
00:04:01,490 --> 00:04:04,260
You are attacking us
because of Kulucahisar!

26
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:07,400
Neither them nor you!

27
00:04:07,980 --> 00:04:11,980
- I only care about justice.
- If you are the banner lord...

28
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:15,340
... then you should've looked after us.

29
00:04:15,770 --> 00:04:17,660
You shouldn't have
come here unnoticed.

30
00:04:17,950 --> 00:04:22,580
Enough, Osman. I won't
learn manners from you.

31
00:04:24,290 --> 00:04:26,250
I can take all of your heads right now!

32
00:04:28,970 --> 00:04:31,190
What do you think you are doing here?

33
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:36,150
Osman killed Kalonoz, he's going
to pay for it, now move aside.

34
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:44,570
Don't you know that we
won't give Osman to you?

35
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:48,490
Are you going to stop me?

36
00:04:50,250 --> 00:04:51,200
Move!

37
00:04:58,770 --> 00:05:03,360
Is it tradition to ambush
Bey's Tent, to draw swords?

38
00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:08,100
We aren't ambushing the Tent,
Abdurrahman Gazi, we are doing our duties.

39
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:25,910
If you are innocent, why are you
standing behind the swords?

40
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:28,780
Do you fear my inquiry?

41
00:05:30,230 --> 00:05:35,070
I don't fear anything that I can see.

42
00:05:38,090 --> 00:05:42,640
But I fear treachery, Alişar Bey.

43
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:49,270
Do you think I will sacrifice
you for an infidel woman?

44
00:05:51,110 --> 00:05:52,990
I will establish a fair trial.

45
00:05:54,830 --> 00:06:01,530
Osman, there are Byzantine,
Mongols, I don't want any more trouble.

46
00:06:02,390 --> 00:06:04,140
Make up your mind.

47
00:06:05,450 --> 00:06:08,960
I am not afraid of your
trial or your judgment.

48
00:06:10,550 --> 00:06:11,460
But...

49
00:06:13,510 --> 00:06:15,840
... I would want to speak
to Sofia face to face.

50
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:21,040
Osman, don't you trust this man.

51
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:25,900
Osman, you don't have to go, my nephew.

52
00:06:26,820 --> 00:06:33,440
We will defend you until Kayı's last
sword, until our last drop of blood.

53
00:06:44,390 --> 00:06:50,080
Both I and my weapon
are on your hands, Alişar Bey.

54
00:07:25,020 --> 00:07:30,760
Alişar Bey, New Bazaar was attacked last
night, our men were slaughtered.

55
00:07:31,750 --> 00:07:33,710
Who did this, Nizamettin?

56
00:07:34,410 --> 00:07:36,300
I will go to the New Bazaar too.

57
00:07:43,790 --> 00:07:47,790
Take him to the mansion,
he will wait in a cell until I return.

58
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:01,250
Osman Bey.

59
00:08:06,130 --> 00:08:07,410
Soldiers!

60
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:41,170
Is it better to fear death,
or wait for the death, Bala?

61
00:08:44,230 --> 00:08:48,230
It was your first dhikr.
I don't know my Sheikh.

62
00:08:56,700 --> 00:09:00,700
Sultan of the brave men, Hz. Hamza...

63
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:08,990
... started to appear in the battles
without an armor near his death.

64
00:09:11,370 --> 00:09:15,370
This move didn't go unnoticed
between the people.

65
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:20,070
Some of them asked: "Oh, master of
swordsmanship didn't you read...

66
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:28,100
... Allah's "do not throw [yourselves] with
your [own] hands into destruction" surah?"

67
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:29,680
Surah Al-Baqarah [2:195]

68
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:34,250
Hz. Hamza answered with wisdom.

69
00:09:34,550 --> 00:09:39,930
"When I was young, I saw death
as a goodbye to this world.

70
00:09:42,650 --> 00:09:48,970
When I was enlightened with
my nephew Hz. Muhammed's light...

71
00:09:49,290 --> 00:09:50,780
... I understood.

72
00:09:52,290 --> 00:09:56,820
That the "do not throw [yourselves] with
your [own] hands into destruction" surah...

73
00:09:56,820 --> 00:10:02,410
... is for the ones who
see death as a danger."

74
00:10:05,790 --> 00:10:15,070
Thus, death is not an end. It is a beginning
about the opening of the gate of truth.

75
00:10:16,890 --> 00:10:25,220
If we know it like this, we would be
waiting for death, not fearing it.

76
00:10:28,850 --> 00:10:34,040
In this period of time, the ones who
will open the gates of conquests...

77
00:10:34,490 --> 00:10:36,910
... won't be the ones who fear death...

78
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:43,510
... but will be the ones who come from
Hz. Hamza, who killed death itself.

79
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:52,370
How good those soldiers are, for they are
not afraid of losing their lives or wealth.

80
00:10:53,350 --> 00:11:00,730
How good those soldiers are, for they
don't choose their desires over their fights.

81
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:06,770
How good those soldiers are, for their
names will be...

82
00:11:07,550 --> 00:11:13,350
... given to a generation, an age, a soul.

83
00:11:57,310 --> 00:11:59,770
Who do you think you are fooling?

84
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:04,730
Do you think you can get away
from me with your lies?

85
00:12:07,910 --> 00:12:09,740
I earned your wrath.

86
00:12:10,890 --> 00:12:15,910
I only wish to be a Muslim
in my last breath.

87
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:32,360
You martyred my Aybars, you burned
my heart, you killed my son!

88
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:39,240
My life is on your hands, Bamsı
Bey. But if you spare me...

89
00:12:43,530 --> 00:12:45,880
... I will be a son to you until I die.

90
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:09,150
Please, give your blessings to me.

91
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:17,900
I took your son from you, Bamsı Bey.

92
00:13:22,390 --> 00:13:24,390
Do what needs to be done.

93
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:06,800
Killing Kulucahisar's general...

94
00:14:07,890 --> 00:14:11,330
... and throwing his body in front
of the castle like an animal, huh?

95
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:17,010
I will make you pay such a price...

96
00:14:19,170 --> 00:14:21,950
... that everyone will
hear about it, Osman.

97
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:27,200
First Osman, then all of the Kayı.

98
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:31,540
After them, every single
one of the Turks...

99
00:14:31,990 --> 00:14:37,440
... I will rip every one of their
hearts and feed it to the dogs!

100
00:14:39,170 --> 00:14:43,180
I swear, not only for Kalonoz...

101
00:14:43,630 --> 00:14:51,570
...I will kill tens of Turks for every
one of our soldiers that we've lost!

102
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:54,640
Alişar Bey must've taken
Osman from his Tent.

103
00:14:55,070 --> 00:14:58,450
We can't touch Kayıs before he's dead.

104
00:14:58,580 --> 00:15:03,740
Even if Alişar Bey took Osman from
the Kayıs, he can't hold him for long.

105
00:15:05,010 --> 00:15:08,200
Osman will find a way to break free.

106
00:15:40,580 --> 00:15:42,040
Samsa Bey.

107
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:50,840
Don't let us spill our
brothers' blood, Zorba.

108
00:15:51,070 --> 00:15:52,670
Let Osman Bey go.

109
00:15:52,990 --> 00:15:56,990
We are just obeying orders, Samsa Bey.
Don't make this hard for us.

110
00:15:57,210 --> 00:16:03,790
Well then, if anyone wants to draw
their last breath, take up your swords!

111
00:16:04,490 --> 00:16:07,790
I said it once, I won't
say it again, Zorba!

112
00:16:12,710 --> 00:16:14,330
Then come and take him!

113
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:26,580
Brothers!

114
00:16:27,710 --> 00:16:29,670
Put down your swords.

115
00:16:30,610 --> 00:16:32,260
Don't make Alps angry.

116
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:34,730
You will get yourselves killed.

117
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:07,120
Don't make these brave men's
knots tight, Brother Bora.

118
00:17:07,410 --> 00:17:08,700
Or they will die here.

119
00:17:09,010 --> 00:17:10,540
On your command, my Bey!

120
00:17:37,300 --> 00:17:38,760
Thank you, Sergeant Samsa.

121
00:17:47,270 --> 00:17:50,890
I can't wait to watch Osman die.

122
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:58,220
You are right, but we should prepare
our game, in case he gets away.

123
00:17:58,790 --> 00:18:04,800
My informant Nizamettin brought
me very important news.

124
00:18:05,030 --> 00:18:09,030
Alişar fell in love with
Edebali's daughter.

125
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:19,390
Only this is enough to make
Alişar and Osman fight each other.

126
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:26,410
But don't forget, if Osman gave in
to Alişar, he must have a plan.

127
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:32,270
We must tread very carefully.

128
00:18:35,230 --> 00:18:38,650
Isn't there any word from Salvador yet?

129
00:18:38,760 --> 00:18:40,040
No, sir.

130
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:23,080
"I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the messenger of Allah."

131
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:38,520
"I bear witness that there
is no deity but Allah...

132
00:19:41,900 --> 00:19:45,000
"I bear witness that there
is no deity but Allah...

133
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:48,190
... and I bear witness...

134
00:19:49,110 --> 00:19:50,510
... and I bear witness...

135
00:19:50,730 --> 00:19:54,860
...that Muhammad is the
messenger of Allah."

136
00:19:55,380 --> 00:19:58,590
...that Muhammad is the
messenger of Allah."

137
00:20:20,210 --> 00:20:22,160
What are we going to do now, Osman bey?

138
00:20:23,190 --> 00:20:26,970
Alişar Bey has been taking gold from
Konya, under the Mongol invasion.

139
00:20:27,410 --> 00:20:29,730
I heard while soldiers were talking.

140
00:20:30,340 --> 00:20:33,490
Then, it is loot time, my Bey.

141
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:39,080
Alişar Bey's gold is halal for those
who worry about the Turks, Osman Bey.

142
00:20:40,870 --> 00:20:45,630
Turks' destiny will be determined not by
the ones who take gold from the enemy...

143
00:20:46,690 --> 00:20:53,880
... but by the ones who sacrifice their
lives and their wealth for this cause.

144
00:20:56,580 --> 00:20:57,980
Sergeant Samsa.

145
00:20:58,540 --> 00:21:03,090
Tell Abdurrahman Gazi. You should take
over the gold with the Alps at once.

146
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:07,180
But, don't let anyone
know it was us for now.

147
00:21:07,390 --> 00:21:09,490
Don't you worry, Osman Bey.

148
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:14,290
- Brother Konur, what about Samsa Bey?
- He hasn't returned yet, my Bey.

149
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:16,890
Let's go here before he kills Salvador.

150
00:21:17,170 --> 00:21:21,170
He has the key to Sofia.
May our fortune be good!

151
00:21:21,260 --> 00:21:24,020
- Allah is Great!
- Allah is One!

152
00:21:24,210 --> 00:21:27,020
- Allah is Great!
- Allah is One!

153
00:21:29,970 --> 00:21:35,520
Hatuns, I don't want Tent's morale to
be low because of Alişar's doings.

154
00:21:36,250 --> 00:21:42,200
You are responsible for
women's happiness and order.

155
00:21:42,670 --> 00:21:43,890
Idiot.

156
00:21:44,410 --> 00:21:49,520
He made friends with Kulucahisar,
he's accompanying them like a dog.

157
00:21:50,170 --> 00:21:51,930
Don't worry, Dündar Bey.

158
00:21:52,250 --> 00:21:56,760
He has gone too far with his last doings.

159
00:21:56,890 --> 00:22:02,970
He slapped my Batur, we stood silent.
But when it is Osman, he has gone too far!

160
00:22:04,150 --> 00:22:05,260
You...

161
00:22:06,290 --> 00:22:08,400
... see a slap when you look.

162
00:22:08,850 --> 00:22:16,080
But I see migration roads,
exiles, taken heads.

163
00:22:17,460 --> 00:22:19,380
Of course we didn't stand silent.

164
00:22:20,130 --> 00:22:24,520
Of course, we had his name on the list.

165
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:29,290
You, you should wait.

166
00:22:29,430 --> 00:22:34,140
We've become mute waiting like that!

167
00:22:34,470 --> 00:22:38,470
He slapped my valiant boy
like a child in the square.

168
00:22:38,540 --> 00:22:40,930
I feel sorrow when I think about it.

169
00:22:41,350 --> 00:22:48,660
Zöhre, don't you know us, do you
think Alişar will get away with that slap?

170
00:22:49,700 --> 00:22:52,150
Is Batur missing something from Osman?

171
00:22:52,730 --> 00:22:55,870
Is Osman different from Batur,
that we would separate them?

172
00:22:56,360 --> 00:22:58,890
Both Osman and Batur are our children.

173
00:22:59,550 --> 00:23:02,550
Thank you Selcan Hatun, thank you.

174
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:05,010
It's like you said, of course.

175
00:23:05,390 --> 00:23:08,330
If we say stop, we say have patience.

176
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:18,020
When the time comes, Kayı's weapons will
cut those hands that slap and chain!

177
00:23:21,710 --> 00:23:24,500
Let it be known like this.

178
00:23:39,410 --> 00:23:41,390
Peace be upon you, Sheikh Edebali.

179
00:23:42,070 --> 00:23:46,070
Peace be upon you too, what is it...

180
00:23:46,260 --> 00:23:48,130
... with all these men, Alişar Bey?

181
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:53,790
Our existence is an example of order.
We are here for order.

182
00:23:55,870 --> 00:23:58,740
Bad things happened at night time.

183
00:23:59,210 --> 00:24:00,960
Do you know anything about it?

184
00:24:20,270 --> 00:24:23,150
- Good news?
- A few of my men were killed...

185
00:24:23,150 --> 00:24:26,550
... by the bandits who attacked
the bazaar.

186
00:24:27,450 --> 00:24:29,970
Have you heard anything about this?

187
00:25:02,890 --> 00:25:06,890
Ablution will cleanse your sins.

188
00:25:08,130 --> 00:25:12,090
Now, wash inside of your ears with
your little fingers...

189
00:25:12,090 --> 00:25:15,890
... back of your neck with the back
of your hand...

190
00:25:15,890 --> 00:25:18,130
... and then your feet.

191
00:25:38,940 --> 00:25:43,930
- May Allah accept it.
- May you live long, Osman. Thank you

192
00:26:09,640 --> 00:26:11,290
Here.

193
00:26:20,600 --> 00:26:24,600
Guys, before you ask...

194
00:26:25,650 --> 00:26:27,750
... I'll tell you.

195
00:26:36,770 --> 00:26:41,460
Just like Wahshi, who killed...

196
00:26:42,900 --> 00:26:45,910
... our prophet Hz. Muhammed's uncle
Hz. Hamza...

197
00:26:46,630 --> 00:26:50,990
... saw reason and became Hz. Wahshi.

198
00:26:51,700 --> 00:26:56,620
- But my Bey!
- Konur! Konur! Konur Alp! Listen to me!

199
00:26:56,910 --> 00:26:59,660
Listen to me! Listen to me!

200
00:26:59,660 --> 00:27:05,590
My son Aybars was a valiant.
He was a valiant.

201
00:27:05,830 --> 00:27:09,830
But was he such a valiant like Prophet
Mohammad's...

202
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:12,960
... uncle Hz. Hamza was?

203
00:27:25,570 --> 00:27:27,570
Our Prophet...

204
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:31,970
... forgave his uncle's killer.

205
00:27:34,350 --> 00:27:37,630
I am a poor Bamsı Beyrek.

206
00:27:40,270 --> 00:27:46,480
As long as there are valiants like you,
who can hinder our cause, Bamsı Bey?

207
00:27:48,470 --> 00:27:50,780
My Osman...

208
00:27:54,350 --> 00:28:01,180
My Bey, what if this infidel is lying
because he fears death?

209
00:28:01,180 --> 00:28:03,470
We'll figure it out now.

210
00:28:09,830 --> 00:28:12,240
His first trial will be harsh.

211
00:28:23,160 --> 00:28:25,870
May Allah forgive their mistakes.

212
00:28:26,410 --> 00:28:29,100
We sleep early and wake up early.

213
00:28:29,830 --> 00:28:32,350
That's what Prophets do.

214
00:28:32,350 --> 00:28:36,530
Interesting. We thought you stay awake
in your sleep...

215
00:28:36,530 --> 00:28:40,350
... alert, and sharp-sighted.

216
00:28:46,030 --> 00:28:51,840
Then you probably don't know that
Osman Bey killed Kalonoz.

217
00:29:00,160 --> 00:29:03,750
Why does the death of a known
infidel like Kalonoz's death...

218
00:29:03,750 --> 00:29:06,660
... disturb you so much, Alişar Bey?

219
00:29:08,230 --> 00:29:11,480
Don't assume I don't know that
you're working with Osman.

220
00:29:14,050 --> 00:29:18,190
I'm asking if you have anything to do
with this incident or not.

221
00:29:18,660 --> 00:29:23,010
Being side by side with a valiant
like Osman is happiness.

222
00:29:24,510 --> 00:29:27,610
I can't say anything about how bold he is.

223
00:29:27,890 --> 00:29:30,020
But he is his own master.

224
00:29:34,070 --> 00:29:40,260
Eagles cannot be caged, lions don't
fit into the jungle, Alişar Bey.

225
00:29:41,140 --> 00:29:43,860
These lands' order is my business.

226
00:29:43,860 --> 00:29:48,820
I don't care about lions or eagles.
The Mongol in Konya doesn't want disorder.

227
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:56,110
Allah knows what really happened
at night, Alişar Bey.

228
00:29:56,580 --> 00:29:59,740
But I know this.

229
00:30:01,420 --> 00:30:05,180
If you add water to the soil,
it becomes mud...

230
00:30:06,550 --> 00:30:09,870
If you add blood,
it becomes your homeland.

231
00:30:15,660 --> 00:30:20,380
If Osman killed that infidel,
well done to him.

232
00:30:21,060 --> 00:30:23,180
He is a great valiant.

233
00:31:28,950 --> 00:31:31,670
Why is that gillyflower upset?

234
00:31:36,400 --> 00:31:38,920
It's thirsty I suppose.

235
00:31:40,500 --> 00:31:43,660
No one thought about watering it.

236
00:31:45,390 --> 00:31:47,250
It faded away.

237
00:32:06,350 --> 00:32:08,400
May it be easy, ladies.

238
00:32:18,390 --> 00:32:22,940
I've been wanting to decorate my
mansion's walls with chinas.

239
00:32:23,950 --> 00:32:26,850
And I don't know anyone more talented
than you.

240
00:32:27,180 --> 00:32:33,390
Besides, what does our religion say?
"Hire those who deserve it."

241
00:32:34,130 --> 00:32:40,050
The same verse continues with
"When you rule, rule with justice."

242
00:32:42,600 --> 00:32:47,910
Isn't Bala Hatun's companionship
a grace, Gonca Hatun?

243
00:32:48,910 --> 00:32:52,710
Her knowledge, her skills...

244
00:32:53,800 --> 00:32:56,660
How wonderful!

245
00:32:57,390 --> 00:33:03,210
I'll definitely trust you with
my mansion, Bala Hatun.

246
00:33:05,730 --> 00:33:10,140
When our skilful Ahis arrive, you can
speak to them about this, Alişar Bey.

247
00:33:10,530 --> 00:33:13,760
I don't paint mansion walls.

248
00:33:21,880 --> 00:33:23,730
Alişar Bey.

249
00:33:24,220 --> 00:33:26,130
What, Nizamettin?

250
00:33:27,110 --> 00:33:30,120
Kayı's Alps rescued Osman Bey from
the soldiers.

251
00:33:32,510 --> 00:33:34,750
What the hell are you talking about?

252
00:34:14,780 --> 00:34:17,590
- I'll pour it, my Sheikh.
- May you live long, my daughter.

253
00:34:25,330 --> 00:34:28,310
- My Sheikh?
- Yes, my daughter?

254
00:34:28,310 --> 00:34:31,410
Nizamettin brought some news as
Alişar Bey was leaving.

255
00:34:32,040 --> 00:34:35,440
He said Osman ran away from the soldiers.

256
00:34:36,040 --> 00:34:40,040
Alişar Bey got angry and left. What is
happening my Sheikh?

257
00:34:42,590 --> 00:34:47,800
Alişar Bey arrested Osman Bey
for killing Kalonoz.

258
00:34:48,780 --> 00:34:50,690
Arrested him?

259
00:34:51,170 --> 00:34:54,730
So Osman Bey ran away from them.

260
00:34:55,340 --> 00:34:57,560
He surely knows something.

261
00:34:57,560 --> 00:35:00,030
What if something happens to
Osman Bey, my Sheikh?

262
00:35:02,710 --> 00:35:04,180
Bala!

263
00:35:04,790 --> 00:35:08,790
Since when do we worry about people?

264
00:35:10,320 --> 00:35:12,900
Allah knows what will happen.

265
00:35:18,470 --> 00:35:20,980
Instead of worrying about Osman...

266
00:35:22,080 --> 00:35:25,520
... you shall mind your own business.
Don't get involved!

267
00:35:29,610 --> 00:35:31,610
Pour some more.

268
00:36:16,210 --> 00:36:18,540
the Mongols have come to the
caravansary, Madam.

269
00:36:35,840 --> 00:36:38,840
You seem to take good care of your fish.

270
00:36:39,710 --> 00:36:42,150
They need me.

271
00:36:43,240 --> 00:36:48,110
Taking care of those who need me,
is in my nature.

272
00:36:49,070 --> 00:36:52,610
Under your stiff looks...

273
00:36:53,570 --> 00:36:57,080
... there is a kind spirit, Alişar Bey.

274
00:37:00,010 --> 00:37:04,720
Just like these fish, you live in a small
pond called Kulucahisar.

275
00:37:06,730 --> 00:37:09,460
My kindness is also for you.

276
00:37:15,950 --> 00:37:19,590
As much as we needed your kindness...

277
00:37:20,230 --> 00:37:23,640
... surely you needed us.

278
00:37:26,980 --> 00:37:28,730
Princess...

279
00:37:29,950 --> 00:37:34,140
For a smile of yours, for a nice word...

280
00:37:34,850 --> 00:37:38,850
... I've opened doors in my lands bigger
than you can imagine.

281
00:37:39,870 --> 00:37:43,640
If you want to trade, we will
until the end.

282
00:37:44,050 --> 00:37:48,320
If you want Osman, just ask
and I'll skin him.

283
00:37:49,740 --> 00:37:54,770
If a single mistake, a single shadow
comes between us...

284
00:37:55,570 --> 00:37:58,920
Your soldiers haven't brought
Osman Bey yet.

285
00:38:01,130 --> 00:38:05,200
I hope he didn't slip through
your fingers.

286
00:38:08,160 --> 00:38:09,770
Alişar Bey.

287
00:38:31,390 --> 00:38:33,290
Damn it!

288
00:38:34,860 --> 00:38:38,520
Salvador! Go to Master Yannis now!

289
00:38:38,520 --> 00:38:41,590
Tell him that Princess Sofia fell into
Osmans trap. Now!

290
00:39:39,170 --> 00:39:41,070
Where are my soldiers?

291
00:39:42,490 --> 00:39:45,880
I've loosened the ropes. They will be
here shortly.

292
00:39:46,250 --> 00:39:49,050
Why shouldn't I hang you with those ropes?

293
00:39:53,080 --> 00:39:54,650
Soldiers!

294
00:40:05,630 --> 00:40:08,510
Revolt against my rule, huh?

295
00:40:11,170 --> 00:40:15,040
With your boldness, you've
asked for your death.

296
00:40:17,140 --> 00:40:20,260
I've come because I had faith in
your fairness, Alişar Bey.

297
00:40:20,620 --> 00:40:23,950
And now, I give in to your fairness.

298
00:40:49,290 --> 00:40:52,900
What do these mean, Alişar Bey?

299
00:40:54,560 --> 00:40:56,430
What is it, Sofia?

300
00:40:57,620 --> 00:40:59,910
Don't you remember Salvador?

301
00:41:08,900 --> 00:41:11,890
I'm seeing this man for
the first time in my life.

302
00:41:13,860 --> 00:41:15,550
Is that so?

303
00:41:17,710 --> 00:41:19,740
Let me remind you then.

304
00:41:22,400 --> 00:41:24,240
Salvador, leader of the Catalans...

305
00:41:24,240 --> 00:41:28,140
... who attacked New Bazaar under you
and your father's command.

306
00:41:38,090 --> 00:41:42,170
- Is that true, Sofia?
- How can you believe Osman's lies?

307
00:41:42,360 --> 00:41:45,630
- How can you prove yourself?
- Alişar Bey!

308
00:41:46,650 --> 00:41:49,970
All the gold we got from attacking
your Bazaar...

309
00:41:51,120 --> 00:41:53,300
... are still in my secret place.

310
00:41:54,300 --> 00:41:58,390
I'm ready to go there with your soldiers
and give them back to you.

311
00:42:02,240 --> 00:42:07,870
But Salvador still has some things
to say, Alişar Bey.

312
00:42:08,440 --> 00:42:10,620
There's still lots of things you'll hear.

313
00:42:10,620 --> 00:42:12,110
Enough!

314
00:42:14,020 --> 00:42:17,240
I can't stand this shamelessness anymore!

315
00:42:19,720 --> 00:42:21,010
I'm leaving.

316
00:42:22,930 --> 00:42:24,880
Wait for a second, Sofia.

317
00:42:25,370 --> 00:42:29,920
You wanted a court, here it is.

318
00:42:31,740 --> 00:42:34,240
- Soldiers!
- Betrayal!

319
00:43:05,140 --> 00:43:06,780
Alişar Bey!

320
00:43:07,650 --> 00:43:09,560
Alişar Bey.

321
00:43:23,370 --> 00:43:24,860
Osman.

322
00:43:26,990 --> 00:43:28,500
Leave her alone.

323
00:43:33,450 --> 00:43:35,780
I want to learn everything you know.

324
00:43:36,680 --> 00:43:38,810
Tell me everything.

325
00:43:59,240 --> 00:44:03,010
I've been walking for two days.
I'm hungry. Please, a piece of bread.

326
00:44:09,390 --> 00:44:10,790
Take a seat.

327
00:44:26,770 --> 00:44:30,670
- Thanks, brother.
- He can't hear you. He's mute and deaf.

328
00:44:54,560 --> 00:44:57,610
Prepare a meal for us!
And take four servings to the room!

329
00:44:58,070 --> 00:44:59,550
Okay.

330
00:45:06,740 --> 00:45:11,880
Abdurrahman Gazi. You take care of the
ones inside with Erkut Alp.

331
00:45:12,310 --> 00:45:16,940
The gold is probably in the room. We'll go
to the room with Boğaç brother.

332
00:45:17,140 --> 00:45:20,990
You know what to do.
Let them attack first.

333
00:45:25,010 --> 00:45:26,910
Good luck.

334
00:46:07,450 --> 00:46:09,290
What do you think you're doing?

335
00:46:10,260 --> 00:46:11,830
I'll strangle you!

336
00:46:14,760 --> 00:46:16,280
He's mine.

337
00:46:18,260 --> 00:46:20,160
He stole my stuff!

338
00:46:35,480 --> 00:46:39,460
So Yorgopolos' killers are
Sofia and Kalonoz.

339
00:46:39,920 --> 00:46:41,390
Is that correct?

340
00:46:52,210 --> 00:46:55,920
A bandit Osman Bey bought with gold...

341
00:46:56,740 --> 00:47:01,540
... is slandering me while hiding
behind your holy religion.

342
00:47:05,150 --> 00:47:09,370
Will you still keep silent, Alişar Bey?

343
00:47:10,580 --> 00:47:18,340
Your dreams with Yannis will be crushed
under Kulucahisar's debris, Sofia!

344
00:47:19,990 --> 00:47:22,180
I have witnessed everything.

345
00:47:23,190 --> 00:47:27,520
I am ready to witness in the presence of
Emperor.

346
00:47:30,460 --> 00:47:34,080
There are so many evidence to prove
in the castle.

347
00:47:34,470 --> 00:47:39,340
We just need to get through the walls,
Alişar Bey.

348
00:47:42,580 --> 00:47:46,020
When this vile game ends and
you come back to my castle...

349
00:47:47,550 --> 00:47:53,950
you'll fear Emperor's anger, Alişar.

350
00:48:02,440 --> 00:48:04,940
You too, Salvador.

351
00:48:05,810 --> 00:48:11,010
You'll be sorry.

352
00:48:11,010 --> 00:48:15,700
I would be honored to die.

353
00:48:15,760 --> 00:48:20,160
I will die as a martyr, Sofia.

354
00:48:29,500 --> 00:48:31,920
This game ends here.

355
00:48:33,600 --> 00:48:39,060
Kill me, or let me go, Alişar Bey!

356
00:48:39,150 --> 00:48:42,030
There is a lot to talk about.

357
00:48:43,290 --> 00:48:47,810
Soldiers!
Take her to the dungeon!

358
00:48:47,910 --> 00:48:50,840
Get your hands off me!

359
00:48:51,320 --> 00:48:57,590
Get off!
I'll see you and your tent again, Osman!

360
00:49:05,550 --> 00:49:09,700
Alişar Bey.
Salvador is a Muslim now.

361
00:49:11,470 --> 00:49:18,790
He is under my protection. If you allow,
he can bring the new bazaar's golds.

362
00:49:22,860 --> 00:49:26,300
I trust your words, Osman Bey.

363
00:49:28,660 --> 00:49:32,810
Bamsı Bey, set off immediately.

364
00:49:32,810 --> 00:49:35,090
Eyvallah(okay), my Osman.

365
00:50:05,930 --> 00:50:08,690
This is for you.

366
00:50:08,690 --> 00:50:12,050
Leave the food and get out.
Now!

367
00:50:58,990 --> 00:51:00,990
Ignoble Alişar!

368
00:51:01,500 --> 00:51:06,080
He lost his faith to reach the infidel's
gold!

369
00:51:06,570 --> 00:51:10,370
He is trying to rule the Turks with
their gold!

370
00:51:12,080 --> 00:51:15,680
Your turn will come!

371
00:51:28,310 --> 00:51:30,800
Alişar Bey will kill me.

372
00:51:31,250 --> 00:51:33,690
Sofia fooled all of us.

373
00:51:36,380 --> 00:51:42,860
She fooled us with her poisoned tongue.

374
00:51:45,080 --> 00:51:47,440
If you were like the old...

375
00:51:48,160 --> 00:51:52,960
Alişar Bey, I would tell you everything.

376
00:51:53,450 --> 00:51:57,340
However, you were stunned by Sofia and
you wouldn't have understood me...

377
00:51:57,340 --> 00:51:59,620
even if I'd told you.

378
00:52:06,580 --> 00:52:09,820
Everything was to protect our land.

379
00:52:10,470 --> 00:52:14,400
- Sofia poisoned all of us.
- Not only Sofia.

380
00:52:15,050 --> 00:52:17,930
Also his father Yannis did.

381
00:52:20,050 --> 00:52:23,790
I'll take him from that castle.

382
00:52:23,830 --> 00:52:30,210
Either they give him to me right away,
or I'll do it by force, Yannis!

383
00:52:31,580 --> 00:52:33,530
Believe me.

384
00:52:39,660 --> 00:52:42,950
Listen to me very carefully, Alişar Bey.

385
00:52:43,730 --> 00:52:46,940
Sofia is not just the wife of a Tekfur...

386
00:52:47,220 --> 00:52:52,400
And Yannis is not just a random monk.

387
00:52:56,440 --> 00:53:01,740
Osman Bey, you are not only a
valiant Alp...

388
00:53:02,310 --> 00:53:05,010
but also a strong and wise Bey.

389
00:53:05,120 --> 00:53:09,950
I will rule this land with Beys like you.

390
00:53:12,460 --> 00:53:19,760
What I don't understand is, how come
Sheik Edebalı didn't accept you as a groom?

391
00:53:21,450 --> 00:53:24,830
You are like my brother, Osman Bey.

392
00:53:24,900 --> 00:53:27,880
I know you love Bala Hatun.

393
00:53:29,430 --> 00:53:32,510
What are you going to do?
Tell me.

394
00:53:58,840 --> 00:54:04,560
No one can keep me here!

395
00:54:07,290 --> 00:54:10,130
Do you hear me?

396
00:54:48,350 --> 00:54:50,740
Sheik Edebalı is a great scholar.

397
00:54:51,670 --> 00:54:55,870
There must be a reason to refuse a
Kayı Bey...

398
00:54:55,870 --> 00:55:01,420
who faced sufferings for his daughter.

399
00:55:09,790 --> 00:55:14,850
My Bey, Mongols who were carrying the
golds were killed.

400
00:55:15,380 --> 00:55:17,640
What are you talking about?

401
00:55:19,270 --> 00:55:25,760
What do you mean they were killed?
Who dares to do this in my land?

402
00:55:25,760 --> 00:55:28,150
- My Bey...
- What about the gold?

403
00:55:28,150 --> 00:55:30,490
They took the gold, my Bey.

404
00:55:31,640 --> 00:55:35,090
Gather the soldiers!
Search everywhere!

405
00:55:35,090 --> 00:55:38,850
I'll go to the caravanserai.
Get my horse ready, now!

406
00:55:43,330 --> 00:55:46,290
Treason is all over us, Osman Bey.

407
00:55:46,530 --> 00:55:49,490
I'll make those traitors pay!

408
00:55:52,770 --> 00:55:55,670
Don't panic, Alişar Bey.

409
00:55:55,670 --> 00:56:02,370
I'll be on your side when we destroy
the traitor in the Kulucahisar Castle.

410
00:56:28,070 --> 00:56:30,820
Wild dogs!

411
00:56:31,000 --> 00:56:34,600
They think they can stop me by taking
Sofia.

412
00:56:44,100 --> 00:56:50,260
Get my daughter out of that dungeon,
Nizamettin. You know Alişar's mansion well.

413
00:56:50,260 --> 00:56:54,160
- We'll do our best with Helen, sir.
- If something happens to my daughter...

414
00:56:54,160 --> 00:56:58,690
I'll burn you with that mansion!

415
00:56:58,690 --> 00:57:03,360
I will not let any harm touch
Sofia, sir.

416
00:57:03,360 --> 00:57:08,500
Show them who Yannis is!

417
00:57:16,090 --> 00:57:18,870
My bird.
What did you bring me?

418
00:57:18,870 --> 00:57:22,670
Osman's alps.
They got into the caravansarai.

419
00:57:22,820 --> 00:57:27,270
They stole the gold that Mongols
brought to Alişar Bey, Efendi Yannis.

420
00:57:27,750 --> 00:57:34,510
You will take your own life while
trying to kill my daughter, Osman.

421
00:57:36,430 --> 00:57:38,420
Leave!

422
00:57:42,970 --> 00:57:48,530
- What do you think, sir.
- I will meet Alişar in the Caravansarai.

423
00:57:51,480 --> 00:57:53,460
I have heard that...

424
00:57:53,870 --> 00:57:57,240
my father will do appointments, brother.

425
00:58:00,590 --> 00:58:03,280
Who works hard is awarded, my Batur.

426
00:58:03,540 --> 00:58:06,840
Obviously my uncle wants people to work.

427
00:58:07,840 --> 00:58:09,870
I wonder...

428
00:58:10,510 --> 00:58:13,140
where he will appoint everyone.

429
00:58:14,820 --> 00:58:19,520
In Kayı tradition, you don't want a
mission, a mission is given to you.

430
00:58:20,800 --> 00:58:25,870
The valiant who takes the mission
completes it.

431
00:58:26,040 --> 00:58:27,680
That's right.

432
00:58:28,340 --> 00:58:34,810
You're tired, brother. Trading on one hand,
being Head Alp in the other.

433
00:58:35,390 --> 00:58:40,290
What now, my Batur?
Do you want to be the Head Alp?

434
00:58:41,220 --> 00:58:46,780
I didn't mean it, brother. I said it
because you are busy.

435
00:58:49,100 --> 00:58:51,160
Let the joke aside...

436
00:58:52,340 --> 00:58:55,560
Being Head Alp is a hard mission,
my Batur.

437
00:58:55,960 --> 00:58:59,550
Even in Kayı, it is harder.

438
00:59:02,100 --> 00:59:08,080
The mission should be given to a valiant
who is brave like you.

439
00:59:11,330 --> 00:59:15,040
Eyvallah (thank you) brother.
Eyvallah.

440
00:59:17,060 --> 00:59:25,100
However, brave young men cannot succeed
every time, but you do.

441
00:59:27,500 --> 00:59:30,870
If my father will do as we say...

442
00:59:30,890 --> 00:59:37,590
I think he may appoint you as his
assistant because you are experienced.

443
00:59:39,960 --> 00:59:43,310
Hope the best, my Batur.

444
00:59:43,420 --> 00:59:45,650
Hope the best.

445
01:00:13,290 --> 01:00:17,880
Where were you while my men were
being killed...

446
01:00:17,880 --> 01:00:19,870
in the day time?

447
01:00:19,870 --> 01:00:23,240
My Bey, it happened suddenly.
I didn't see anything.

448
01:00:23,250 --> 01:00:26,410
You work in my land...

449
01:00:26,410 --> 01:00:30,100
but you don't see while they
steal my gold!

450
01:00:30,100 --> 01:00:34,930
- Take him! a hundred whips!
- Forgive, my Bey, please.

451
01:00:34,930 --> 01:00:38,470
I am not done with you!

452
01:00:40,450 --> 01:00:44,640
No one saw or heard about you.

453
01:00:45,510 --> 01:00:48,170
Don't they know about my anger?

454
01:00:48,170 --> 01:00:52,980
I will find them even if the ground
swallows them.

455
01:00:52,980 --> 01:00:55,390
I will find them!

456
01:01:08,890 --> 01:01:15,020
Some can see the invisible, and hear
the inaudible.

457
01:01:15,350 --> 01:01:17,440
Who are you, old man?

458
01:01:17,440 --> 01:01:21,770
My name is Astrologer Abdül, my Bey.

459
01:01:22,330 --> 01:01:27,510
I can see the deep.
I see the future.

460
01:01:29,370 --> 01:01:31,440
Take him out!

461
01:01:31,680 --> 01:01:34,420
You are looking for who did this!

462
01:01:34,420 --> 01:01:36,350
Stop!

463
01:01:48,960 --> 01:01:55,450
There are eyes which can see but
cannot talk.

464
01:01:59,720 --> 01:02:02,380
What are you talking about, old man?

465
01:02:02,390 --> 01:02:07,210
Say what you have to say!

466
01:02:07,210 --> 01:02:11,640
Deaf and mute.

467
01:02:11,660 --> 01:02:15,040
But he sees like an eagle!

468
01:02:15,040 --> 01:02:18,390
Who is that?

469
01:02:18,410 --> 01:02:21,640
My Bey, there is a poor around here.

470
01:02:21,650 --> 01:02:24,530
- Where is he?
- He lives in the yard.

471
01:02:24,530 --> 01:02:27,060
Bring him to me immediately!

472
01:03:06,060 --> 01:03:08,930
Eat!
This is your last meal.

473
01:04:27,640 --> 01:04:29,950
Who did this?

474
01:04:30,460 --> 01:04:34,900
Are you ready to see the truth,
Alişar Bey?

475
01:05:14,920 --> 01:05:16,830
Kayıs!

476
01:05:39,160 --> 01:05:41,230
Take him out.

477
01:05:52,690 --> 01:05:54,990
So, Abdul.

478
01:05:56,640 --> 01:06:01,160
We have never heard of you.

479
01:06:01,550 --> 01:06:05,920
We are having a lot of trouble.

480
01:06:07,240 --> 01:06:11,830
May you bring good news, old man.

481
01:06:27,370 --> 01:06:32,050
This gold glints.

482
01:06:35,680 --> 01:06:40,480
However, your fate is dark.

483
01:06:45,160 --> 01:06:48,730
I see a mansion.

484
01:06:49,190 --> 01:06:55,590
Beyond misty roads and gauzy hills.

485
01:06:56,040 --> 01:07:00,820
A great mansion.

486
01:07:01,670 --> 01:07:07,270
And a prisoner who is getting ready to
escape.

487
01:07:09,180 --> 01:07:12,270
Delicate like a flower...

488
01:07:12,270 --> 01:07:18,210
but wild inside, a prisoner.

489
01:07:20,480 --> 01:07:23,220
You see the deep, old man.

490
01:07:23,840 --> 01:07:26,480
But you miss one thing.

491
01:07:26,480 --> 01:07:32,100
My mansion is more secure than
the Emperor's castle in Constantinopolis.

492
01:07:32,100 --> 01:07:34,670
Don't forget, Alişar Bey.

493
01:07:34,670 --> 01:07:38,130
The chain holds the prisoner.

494
01:07:39,380 --> 01:07:44,370
But treason breaks the order!

495
01:07:46,100 --> 01:07:50,240
While all of my men guards...

496
01:07:50,240 --> 01:07:57,100
a prisoner aside, even a soul cannot
get out of there.

497
01:07:57,260 --> 01:08:01,350
Just remember my words, Alişar Bey.

498
01:08:01,430 --> 01:08:06,480
If you seek for help...

499
01:08:06,780 --> 01:08:11,060
I will be in the cave in Kartalkaya.

500
01:08:36,830 --> 01:08:39,850
What's up, princess?
Didn't you like it?

501
01:08:39,900 --> 01:08:42,930
It's not like the castle's food, right?

502
01:09:59,520 --> 01:10:01,400
More power to you Bala Hatun.

503
01:10:01,930 --> 01:10:04,040
Do it yourself, if it's easy Aygül Hatun.

504
01:10:05,210 --> 01:10:06,420
Your job is hard.

505
01:10:07,170 --> 01:10:10,230
You make two jugs and sweat blood...

506
01:10:10,230 --> 01:10:11,960
...just to gain some money.

507
01:10:12,430 --> 01:10:15,090
The point is gaining honestly,
Aygül Hatun.

508
01:10:15,700 --> 01:10:19,060
A despiser eye would not see
the beauty or effort.

509
01:10:20,670 --> 01:10:23,120
To see beauty, you should look well.

510
01:10:28,200 --> 01:10:30,790
Give me two jugs from there.

511
01:10:30,960 --> 01:10:33,610
Let us play a role in your earning.

512
01:10:34,300 --> 01:10:36,650
I cannot take your money, Burçin Hatun.

513
01:10:38,200 --> 01:10:39,650
What does that mean?

514
01:10:40,950 --> 01:10:42,580
Don't you like us?

515
01:10:44,390 --> 01:10:45,860
I didn't mean it.

516
01:10:46,410 --> 01:10:48,140
We respect Osman Bey very much.

517
01:10:49,330 --> 01:10:52,210
We can't sell you anything, we can
only gift.

518
01:12:47,960 --> 01:12:49,480
Accept it, Aygül Hatun.

519
01:12:50,810 --> 01:12:52,020
I painted it on my own.

520
01:12:52,420 --> 01:12:54,630
Something happened
that made me really happy.

521
01:12:55,060 --> 01:12:57,100
That's why its colours are this vivid.

522
01:12:57,930 --> 01:12:59,690
It's my gift to you.

523
01:13:16,530 --> 01:13:17,910
As-salamu alaykum.
(Peace be unto you)

524
01:13:18,950 --> 01:13:20,420
Alaikum salam.
(Peace be unto you too)

525
01:13:20,530 --> 01:13:21,660
Bala Hatun...

526
01:13:22,090 --> 01:13:23,830
...Osman Bey wants to see you.

527
01:13:24,430 --> 01:13:26,040
He has something to say.

528
01:13:31,240 --> 01:13:31,980
Bala...

529
01:13:36,410 --> 01:13:38,880
... my Sheikh would not want
you to meet him.

530
01:13:38,990 --> 01:13:40,100
Don't you know it?

531
01:13:44,060 --> 01:13:45,540
Will you really go?

532
01:13:45,800 --> 01:13:47,830
Osman Bey is in trouble because of us.

533
01:13:49,040 --> 01:13:51,020
My father doesn't want to see him either.

534
01:13:51,830 --> 01:13:55,600
If it wasn't important,
Osman Bey wouldn't want to see me, Gonca.

535
01:13:55,740 --> 01:13:56,940
I should go and learn it.

536
01:13:57,150 --> 01:13:57,970
See you.

537
01:14:12,830 --> 01:14:13,800
What a pity!

538
01:14:14,390 --> 01:14:15,700
It's broken now.

539
01:14:23,000 --> 01:14:23,800
Don't be upset.

540
01:14:24,890 --> 01:14:27,400
There are much better ones.

541
01:14:29,430 --> 01:14:31,710
Not much effort was put into it anyway.

542
01:14:59,860 --> 01:15:00,880
Osman...

543
01:15:01,820 --> 01:15:04,480
...luckily I could see you unhurt.

544
01:15:05,530 --> 01:15:06,920
My beautiful.

545
01:15:08,610 --> 01:15:09,950
My gracious love.

546
01:15:13,510 --> 01:15:14,450
My sun.

547
01:15:17,140 --> 01:15:18,300
I ate my heart out.

548
01:15:19,840 --> 01:15:21,050
Tell me.

549
01:15:21,280 --> 01:15:22,620
What's going on Osman?

550
01:15:23,930 --> 01:15:26,310
The snake Sofia is at the place
that she deserves.

551
01:15:27,280 --> 01:15:29,200
In Alişar's dungeon.

552
01:15:29,650 --> 01:15:32,000
The infidels will stay away from you
for a whlie.

553
01:15:32,830 --> 01:15:35,200
But I don't know how long it
will be like this.

554
01:15:35,550 --> 01:15:37,340
But we should be awake.

555
01:15:38,290 --> 01:15:40,590
Alişar is giddy-paced, he is unreliable.

556
01:15:42,010 --> 01:15:44,340
He is ignoble and it's really clear.

557
01:15:44,850 --> 01:15:46,420
We won't trust him.

558
01:15:46,700 --> 01:15:47,990
Don't worry.

559
01:15:54,300 --> 01:15:56,460
What is bothering your heart, Bala?

560
01:15:57,820 --> 01:15:58,520
Tell me.

561
01:16:02,530 --> 01:16:03,540
Osman...

562
01:16:06,210 --> 01:16:08,380
...while we're waiting with patience...

563
01:16:09,470 --> 01:16:11,640
...what if another aspirant comes up?

564
01:16:15,830 --> 01:16:17,570
If my father finds it proper...

565
01:16:18,480 --> 01:16:20,010
...I'm afraid Osman.

566
01:16:20,080 --> 01:16:22,530
Your name is sealed to my heart Bala.

567
01:16:22,780 --> 01:16:26,690
I will never love someone else, and
I will never let anybody else love you.

568
01:16:28,210 --> 01:16:29,580
Don't be afraid.

569
01:16:39,680 --> 01:16:41,950
Till I smell your silky hair...

570
01:16:44,190 --> 01:16:45,830
...wear this kerchief.

571
01:16:53,210 --> 01:16:58,090
Any time that I pray to Allah, there is
always your name in my lips.

572
01:16:58,450 --> 01:17:03,150
My pray is that, he gives us to each other
for lifelong.

573
01:17:05,050 --> 01:17:06,130
Inshallah.

574
01:17:08,400 --> 01:17:10,640
May Allah help you.

575
01:17:12,910 --> 01:17:14,750
My prayers are with you.

576
01:17:17,990 --> 01:17:20,520
But my father doesn't want us
to see each other.

577
01:17:24,390 --> 01:17:27,230
From now on, don't call me.

578
01:17:29,430 --> 01:17:30,700
I understand.

579
01:17:33,540 --> 01:17:34,790
I understand, Bala.

580
01:17:35,630 --> 01:17:37,360
Don't bother your heart.

581
01:17:38,310 --> 01:17:39,410
Just pray.

582
01:17:40,540 --> 01:17:42,770
Your prayer is my armor.

583
01:17:53,000 --> 01:17:54,160
Father!

584
01:17:56,510 --> 01:17:57,510
My daughter.

585
01:17:57,860 --> 01:18:01,250
The dog that called Osman
did it again!

586
01:18:03,590 --> 01:18:07,230
Fortunately, your father put
a servant...

587
01:18:07,340 --> 01:18:09,680
...next to everyone who may hurt you.

588
01:18:10,790 --> 01:18:12,020
Father.

589
01:18:12,350 --> 01:18:15,420
After he learns that I escaped,
Alişar Bey will come after me.

590
01:18:16,410 --> 01:18:17,910
How will we stop him?

591
01:18:18,400 --> 01:18:21,550
Alişar Bey met Abdül.

592
01:18:22,660 --> 01:18:26,750
Abdül already told him that
his captive will escape.

593
01:18:28,370 --> 01:18:29,560
Who is Abdül?

594
01:18:31,840 --> 01:18:35,160
The Chaldean
who will make Alişar our puppet.

595
01:18:37,520 --> 01:18:41,110
His one name is Abdül,
and the other name is...

596
01:18:47,120 --> 01:18:47,890
Yannis.

597
01:18:48,620 --> 01:18:49,550
Yannis.

598
01:19:34,390 --> 01:19:36,070
May Allah accept it, father.

599
01:19:37,000 --> 01:19:38,480
Inshallah, my daughter.

600
01:20:08,580 --> 01:20:11,590
Pick up your foods, little lives.

601
01:20:16,830 --> 01:20:18,220
Pick them up.

602
01:20:19,590 --> 01:20:21,790
They are too many to count.

603
01:20:23,180 --> 01:20:24,180
But...

604
01:20:25,000 --> 01:20:26,810
... there is one in the lead.

605
01:20:29,170 --> 01:20:34,680
Wherever it goes, the others follow him.

606
01:20:35,590 --> 01:20:37,120
And you Bala?

607
01:20:39,020 --> 01:20:41,160
Are you like ants?

608
01:20:50,060 --> 01:20:51,740
You have something to tell me.

609
01:20:53,110 --> 01:20:54,360
Say it.

610
01:20:56,260 --> 01:20:57,710
My Sheikh.

611
01:20:58,920 --> 01:21:02,070
If you allow it, I would like to tell you
what Osman Bey is doing.

612
01:21:05,540 --> 01:21:07,710
Firstly, tell me, my daughter Bala.

613
01:21:09,360 --> 01:21:11,830
How do you know what Osman Bey is doing?

614
01:21:12,930 --> 01:21:14,070
My Sheikh...

615
01:21:15,270 --> 01:21:17,810
...you don't accept Osman Bey...

616
01:21:17,950 --> 01:21:20,700
...he told me to inform you.

617
01:21:25,860 --> 01:21:28,380
Sofia is in a dungeon thanks to him.

618
01:21:29,300 --> 01:21:31,780
The infidels won't bother us for a while.

619
01:21:31,780 --> 01:21:33,970
He told you can concentrate
on your trading...

620
01:21:33,970 --> 01:21:35,980
...but stay alert.

621
01:21:48,340 --> 01:21:54,750
How can you meet Osman while you
know that I don't allow it, Bala?

622
01:22:05,580 --> 01:22:09,020
Is it my daughter?

623
01:22:11,430 --> 01:22:13,360
- My Sheikh--
- I'm asking again!

624
01:22:15,850 --> 01:22:20,960
Is the one who ignored me,
who did what I didn't allow...

625
01:22:22,230 --> 01:22:24,070
...who ignored my permission...

626
01:22:25,880 --> 01:22:27,290
... you?

627
01:22:32,890 --> 01:22:33,820
Silence...

628
01:22:34,350 --> 01:22:35,940
...comes from admission.

629
01:22:39,020 --> 01:22:40,650
It's clearly you.

630
01:22:45,350 --> 01:22:47,480
Obviously you...

631
01:22:49,500 --> 01:22:52,040
...don't care about our words...

632
01:22:53,070 --> 01:22:57,830
...you follow your own truths.

633
01:22:59,080 --> 01:23:00,510
Father...

634
01:23:00,510 --> 01:23:01,390
...don't say that.

635
01:23:01,390 --> 01:23:03,040
Now go and think, Bala.

636
01:23:04,920 --> 01:23:12,130
Think, so you correct your mistake
before we separate from being ourselves.

637
01:23:52,740 --> 01:23:54,570
Thanks to Allah we're full.

638
01:23:55,040 --> 01:23:56,930
May Allah give to those who need it.

639
01:23:57,070 --> 01:23:57,790
Amin.

640
01:23:57,810 --> 01:23:59,730
Amin.

641
01:24:05,680 --> 01:24:09,310
When will we solve his circumcision issue
Bamsı Bey?

642
01:24:12,030 --> 01:24:13,490
Which circumcise?

643
01:24:18,640 --> 01:24:21,470
Do you think to be a Muslim is that easy?

644
01:24:22,720 --> 01:24:27,040
You'll lie down under the knife.
Under the knife!

645
01:24:36,100 --> 01:24:37,770
My sons.

646
01:24:45,040 --> 01:24:46,940
Let's solve this issue tomorrow.

647
01:24:47,680 --> 01:24:50,410
Tomorrow?
What do you mean tomorrow?

648
01:24:54,420 --> 01:24:55,890
Bamsı Bey...

649
01:24:56,270 --> 01:24:59,550
...will his name stay as Salvador?

650
01:25:05,880 --> 01:25:07,420
My Osman...

651
01:25:17,980 --> 01:25:21,630
From now on, your name is...

652
01:25:22,770 --> 01:25:25,480
...Ebubekir Sıddık.

653
01:25:25,880 --> 01:25:27,280
Ebubekir Sıddık.

654
01:25:29,550 --> 01:25:32,860
Be loyal to your religion.

655
01:25:35,980 --> 01:25:38,100
Know it like this, children.

656
01:25:42,210 --> 01:25:43,480
Thank you.

657
01:25:44,390 --> 01:25:46,340
We'll get the booty first.

658
01:25:46,340 --> 01:25:51,100
We'll sacrifice lots of goats to celebrate
Sıddık's circumcision.

659
01:25:51,100 --> 01:25:52,190
Right, Bamsı Bey?

660
01:25:53,550 --> 01:25:55,770
Thank you, Konur Alp. Thank you.

661
01:26:03,750 --> 01:26:07,630
My Osman, what will you do
with that much booty?

662
01:26:09,430 --> 01:26:11,820
No matter Muslim or not...

663
01:26:12,090 --> 01:26:14,060
...we will give them to all poor people.

664
01:26:14,710 --> 01:26:20,720
We'll give them to be hope for
all the world.

665
01:26:21,160 --> 01:26:22,550
Mashallah to my Osman.

666
01:26:27,620 --> 01:26:28,830
Boran brother.

667
01:26:30,080 --> 01:26:31,630
Play us your dombra!

668
01:26:32,220 --> 01:26:34,070
Cheer us up.

669
01:26:35,700 --> 01:26:37,240
As you wish, my Bey.

670
01:29:49,930 --> 01:29:51,970
Mashallah to my brave man.

671
01:29:53,350 --> 01:29:54,610
Mashallah.

672
01:29:54,840 --> 01:29:56,190
Thank you, my Bey.

673
01:30:22,020 --> 01:30:22,760
Bala...

674
01:30:23,430 --> 01:30:25,320
...look, today I bought those threads.

675
01:30:25,530 --> 01:30:28,080
They will become very beautiful
things in your hands.

676
01:30:28,680 --> 01:30:31,500
Look at these beautiful blue and green.

677
01:30:34,240 --> 01:30:35,760
Bala?

678
01:30:40,640 --> 01:30:41,620
Bala.

679
01:30:43,140 --> 01:30:44,770
Don't be upset.

680
01:30:44,770 --> 01:30:45,920
Don't worry.

681
01:30:46,240 --> 01:30:47,800
Everything will be okay.

682
01:30:48,050 --> 01:30:49,500
Will it be okay Gonca?

683
01:30:51,010 --> 01:30:53,190
Do you think my father's anger
will vanish?

684
01:30:54,300 --> 01:30:55,750
Sure it will vanish.

685
01:30:57,800 --> 01:31:00,380
Don't you know how much he loves you?

686
01:31:00,930 --> 01:31:01,900
I know.

687
01:31:03,770 --> 01:31:05,620
This is why I'm afraid.

688
01:31:07,190 --> 01:31:08,870
I ignored his word.

689
01:31:10,080 --> 01:31:12,140
My father won't forgive me easily.

690
01:31:14,310 --> 01:31:19,970
Until I find a way to make him forgive me,
each breath will hurt me, Gonca.

691
01:31:31,320 --> 01:31:36,050
How can she escape from the dungeon, from
the hands...

692
01:31:36,280 --> 01:31:39,020
... of my own soldiers.

693
01:31:39,940 --> 01:31:40,900
How?

694
01:31:49,020 --> 01:31:50,170
I asked you.

695
01:31:50,670 --> 01:31:51,910
How could she escape?

696
01:31:52,690 --> 01:31:55,560
My Bey, this is done by someone
from inside.

697
01:31:55,930 --> 01:31:57,510
There is no other explanation.

698
01:31:58,650 --> 01:32:00,930
Are you aware of your words?

699
01:32:00,990 --> 01:32:02,670
This is betrayal.

700
01:32:03,770 --> 01:32:06,440
The chain holds the captive...

701
01:32:06,700 --> 01:32:10,810
...but betrayal breaks the system.

702
01:32:14,880 --> 01:32:16,920
There is an chaldean in caravansary...

703
01:32:16,920 --> 01:32:19,950
...in the cave in Kartalkaynı.
His name is Abdül.

704
01:32:20,070 --> 01:32:21,760
Find and bring him to me
righ now.

705
01:32:22,730 --> 01:32:24,370
I'll do as you order, my Bey.

706
01:32:38,280 --> 01:32:43,320
Your body is here but your mind is
somewhere else, my Bey.

707
01:32:45,510 --> 01:32:47,680
What are you thinking that deeply?

708
01:32:48,820 --> 01:32:51,290
I'm thinking about my Tent's
future, Hatun.

709
01:32:52,810 --> 01:32:56,810
I'm thinking about my
heart's flower Aygül.

710
01:32:57,390 --> 01:32:59,200
What about Aygül?

711
01:33:00,540 --> 01:33:05,360
Alişar is attacking his own kind with
the word of the enemy.

712
01:33:05,970 --> 01:33:08,400
He's doing wrong to us because of an
infidel's word.

713
01:33:08,590 --> 01:33:09,500
On top of it...

714
01:33:09,830 --> 01:33:13,580
He comes to my tent and slaps my
son.

715
01:33:15,460 --> 01:33:18,790
Aygül, my sweet rose.

716
01:33:19,920 --> 01:33:23,810
I refuse my daughter to fade out in
Alişar's garden.

717
01:33:24,160 --> 01:33:25,630
I'll solve this circle.

718
01:33:26,660 --> 01:33:29,540
Tomorrow's meeting is important.

719
01:33:30,290 --> 01:33:34,430
You have an idea but you're not telling
it.

720
01:33:37,030 --> 01:33:38,720
Then I'll tell you, my Zöhre.

721
01:33:39,750 --> 01:33:42,800
From now on there will be a new order in
the Tent.

722
01:33:43,220 --> 01:33:46,670
We'll be such an order that even Mongol...

723
01:33:47,040 --> 01:33:51,170
...won't make difference, not just Alişar.

724
01:33:53,280 --> 01:33:55,990
I have my nephew on my one side...

725
01:33:57,160 --> 01:34:00,210
...my son, Batur on the other side.

726
01:34:01,870 --> 01:34:05,000
And mighty Osman on my back.

727
01:34:06,630 --> 01:34:07,610
Osman.

728
01:34:10,570 --> 01:34:13,530
My Bey, do you hear yourself?

729
01:34:14,270 --> 01:34:15,490
I do, Hatun.

730
01:34:16,400 --> 01:34:17,330
I do.

731
01:34:17,990 --> 01:34:21,750
Tomorrow I'll give him such
a duty that...

732
01:34:22,130 --> 01:34:24,770
... it will both change his
position in the Tent...

733
01:34:24,810 --> 01:34:28,110
...and his responsibility will
get heavier, but...

734
01:34:29,920 --> 01:34:32,390
... I know that he'll succeed.

735
01:34:35,510 --> 01:34:38,060
You're relying on a mad man like Osman.

736
01:34:39,110 --> 01:34:41,610
My Bey, if you ask me, I'll say think
about it again.

737
01:34:45,150 --> 01:34:46,990
There's nothing to think
about, Hatun.

738
01:34:47,750 --> 01:34:51,330
Tomorrow, after giving his duty...

739
01:34:51,750 --> 01:34:54,070
...I'll want such a thing from him that...

740
01:34:55,220 --> 01:35:00,350
...it will bond him more and more to
our Tent and our family.

741
01:35:01,440 --> 01:35:06,160
And will restrain his madness.

742
01:35:06,620 --> 01:35:09,380
So we will ride out the storm.

743
01:35:10,130 --> 01:35:14,650
Then no one will be able to
stand against us.

744
01:35:21,270 --> 01:35:22,480
Say it, my son.

745
01:35:23,710 --> 01:35:25,480
What makes you upset?

746
01:35:26,280 --> 01:35:28,150
It's for sure, you have a problem.

747
01:35:29,660 --> 01:35:30,770
Yes, I do.

748
01:35:32,580 --> 01:35:33,840
I have a problem.

749
01:35:34,470 --> 01:35:37,070
Say it. Let me take care of it.

750
01:35:39,060 --> 01:35:42,740
Talk to Aygül. She shouldn't marry Alişar.

751
01:35:43,400 --> 01:35:45,850
My uncle won't marry them without Aygül's
consent.

752
01:35:46,430 --> 01:35:48,050
Talk her out of this.

753
01:35:48,470 --> 01:35:51,310
He acts differently to Mongols and
infidels!

754
01:35:51,520 --> 01:35:53,810
May devil take him.

755
01:35:53,910 --> 01:35:56,130
Any kind of malice would come from him.

756
01:35:56,640 --> 01:35:59,820
He's going to take our girl and get in our
family, tent.

757
01:36:00,510 --> 01:36:04,140
What should we do aunt? Should we lay a
bed for this evil?

758
01:36:04,700 --> 01:36:06,340
This isn't a love affair.

759
01:36:08,230 --> 01:36:09,880
This is political affair.

760
01:36:10,720 --> 01:36:13,690
You're right but it's improper.

761
01:36:14,030 --> 01:36:16,750
We can't do anything if she's
okay with it.

762
01:36:20,700 --> 01:36:21,760
You're right, aunt.

763
01:36:23,260 --> 01:36:24,210
You're right.

764
01:36:25,600 --> 01:36:27,970
If this infidel takes Aygül...

765
01:36:28,300 --> 01:36:31,680
...not just our family, our tent will be
fouled as well.

766
01:36:33,730 --> 01:36:35,400
He'll ruin everything.

767
01:36:38,960 --> 01:36:40,990
I would prevent it if I can.

768
01:36:41,520 --> 01:36:44,680
But, you're right aunt.

769
01:36:46,260 --> 01:36:48,650
Without Aygül's consent, we can't do
anything.

770
01:36:50,570 --> 01:36:54,510
My wrathful but merciful, Osman.

771
01:36:55,400 --> 01:36:57,540
May Allah reward you.

772
01:37:00,300 --> 01:37:04,210
Tell me about your heart. What's happening
there?

773
01:37:06,300 --> 01:37:08,690
My one side is like delirious storms.

774
01:37:10,680 --> 01:37:12,900
Wants to go over mountains, plains.

775
01:37:16,980 --> 01:37:18,420
And the other side...

776
01:37:19,630 --> 01:37:21,300
...like I have fallen appart.

777
01:37:22,290 --> 01:37:23,750
I have no strength left.

778
01:37:25,790 --> 01:37:28,010
The heart wants its lover to be nearby.

779
01:37:29,800 --> 01:37:32,260
When someone can't meet their loved one...

780
01:37:32,470 --> 01:37:35,270
... they can't relax.

781
01:37:36,300 --> 01:37:38,020
I'll bring Bala here, my aunt.

782
01:37:39,130 --> 01:37:43,100
I'm waiting. Sheikh Edebali didn't
allow it yet.

783
01:37:44,410 --> 01:37:47,540
Maybe one day he'll allow it.

784
01:37:48,860 --> 01:37:50,730
I'll call him father and kiss his hand.

785
01:37:54,170 --> 01:37:55,630
Hopefully, my son.

786
01:37:56,920 --> 01:37:57,930
Hopefully.

787
01:38:09,170 --> 01:38:10,890
In the ninety-nine names of Allah...

788
01:38:11,330 --> 01:38:14,550
...who has the power to create...

789
01:38:15,240 --> 01:38:17,350
...and who fills our hearts with faith.

790
01:38:18,370 --> 01:38:22,180
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name
of Allah, the compassionate, the merciful)

791
01:38:22,550 --> 01:38:24,550
Valiant Beys of Kayı.

792
01:38:25,390 --> 01:38:29,350
We need to refresh ourselves
to stay alive.

793
01:38:30,050 --> 01:38:33,470
Because of this, I'm thinking about a new
duty arrangements...

794
01:38:33,900 --> 01:38:35,820
...as Kayı Bey's deputy.

795
01:38:39,220 --> 01:38:41,570
Kayı's markets...

796
01:38:42,180 --> 01:38:45,760
... caravans and gold...

797
01:38:46,300 --> 01:38:49,450
... will be held responsible from my
nephew Gündüz...

798
01:38:49,750 --> 01:38:53,000
...which I have never doubt of his morals.

799
01:38:54,720 --> 01:38:55,890
As you order, my Bey.

800
01:39:03,410 --> 01:39:05,500
Soldiery needs valiantness...

801
01:39:06,510 --> 01:39:09,250
...valiantness needs bravery.

802
01:39:12,760 --> 01:39:15,310
Head of Kayı Alps will be...

803
01:39:16,520 --> 01:39:19,570
...my dear son, Batur Bey.

804
01:39:27,580 --> 01:39:28,980
Thank you, my Bey father.

805
01:39:39,430 --> 01:39:44,660
With the arrival of Selcan Hatun's tent,
our numbers will increase.

806
01:39:44,970 --> 01:39:46,870
It's not easy to rule a tent.

807
01:39:47,640 --> 01:39:50,790
It needs to have morals, Bey's attitude...

808
01:39:51,580 --> 01:39:54,400
...and know about Kayı.

809
01:39:54,930 --> 01:39:57,940
Because of that, I held my nephew Osman...

810
01:39:58,800 --> 01:40:02,200
... responsible as my Lead Assistant...

811
01:40:03,890 --> 01:40:05,890
... who grew up in my brother's tent.

812
01:40:18,970 --> 01:40:20,440
Order is yours, my Bey.

813
01:40:27,390 --> 01:40:29,010
These our new duties that given...

814
01:40:30,250 --> 01:40:31,680
...for our magnificent tent...

815
01:40:32,900 --> 01:40:37,260
...and our fertile land.

816
01:40:38,510 --> 01:40:41,110
Thank you, my Bey.

817
01:41:08,210 --> 01:41:09,930
My hunting fellows!

818
01:41:10,510 --> 01:41:12,090
My young scouts!

819
01:41:12,880 --> 01:41:16,590
We will start the hunting season
early this year.

820
01:41:19,840 --> 01:41:23,210
Before the flowers bloom...

821
01:41:28,130 --> 01:41:31,020
Before the young ones stop sucking milk...

822
01:41:33,040 --> 01:41:35,130
The blood season has come.

823
01:41:36,070 --> 01:41:39,700
My anger shall be engraved on the
Sultan's shadow Alişar Bey's banner...

824
01:41:41,080 --> 01:41:44,630
... on it's water, on it's soil, it's
rocks.

825
01:41:47,110 --> 01:41:51,330
Those who hurt me should know that
I'll hurt them more!

826
01:41:52,460 --> 01:41:57,200
Those who burn my heart should know that
I'll turn their Tents into ashes!

827
01:41:59,110 --> 01:42:02,520
Now go and spit blood on them!

828
01:42:04,120 --> 01:42:07,200
Show them the power of Alişar Bey!

829
01:42:07,900 --> 01:42:11,180
You'll take Kayıs down when you see them!

830
01:42:25,610 --> 01:42:29,620
What is it, Ayşe Hatun. You look like
you're looking at something beautiful.

831
01:42:30,960 --> 01:42:32,400
I'm looking at my valiant.

832
01:42:33,810 --> 01:42:36,190
I cheer up the more I look, my Gündüz.

833
01:42:37,480 --> 01:42:40,580
I wish your ancestor Süleyman Şah
could see your magnificence.

834
01:42:47,910 --> 01:42:49,180
My sunlight...

835
01:42:50,790 --> 01:42:51,740
... my Ayşe...

836
01:42:54,170 --> 01:42:56,440
If a valiant came out of this Gündüz...

837
01:42:58,410 --> 01:43:01,100
... it's because you were by my side.

838
01:43:02,230 --> 01:43:03,180
Know that.

839
01:43:10,520 --> 01:43:13,030
May Allah help you with your work, my Bey.

840
01:43:13,630 --> 01:43:16,350
Hopefully, Hatun.

841
01:43:19,720 --> 01:43:22,750
A cart full of goods are ready.

842
01:43:23,010 --> 01:43:27,770
Now we shall go to the Bazaar and get
what we deserve.

843
01:43:29,260 --> 01:43:30,230
My Gündüz...

844
01:43:35,000 --> 01:43:36,810
Don't take this out of your neck.

845
01:43:38,960 --> 01:43:42,400
My Allah shall both protect you...

846
01:43:43,710 --> 01:43:45,530
... and make hard things easy for you.

847
01:43:45,610 --> 01:43:46,730
Hopefully.

848
01:43:51,940 --> 01:43:53,280
Thank you, Hatun.

849
01:44:03,240 --> 01:44:04,600
May Allah protect you.

850
01:44:05,040 --> 01:44:06,020
You too.

851
01:44:06,820 --> 01:44:08,290
My prayers are with you.

852
01:45:08,860 --> 01:45:09,750
Grandfather!

853
01:45:22,930 --> 01:45:25,260
May Allah bless those who left this!

854
01:46:04,760 --> 01:46:06,680
Do you want to hear a secret, Karayel?

855
01:46:08,470 --> 01:46:10,190
No one knows this.

856
01:46:12,360 --> 01:46:13,550
You should know it.

857
01:46:16,840 --> 01:46:18,400
I promised something.

858
01:46:20,300 --> 01:46:21,440
A long time ago.

859
01:46:22,200 --> 01:46:25,670
Maybe before I was even born.

860
01:46:26,730 --> 01:46:30,110
I said "My name is Osman!"

861
01:46:31,370 --> 01:46:35,590
"I will put my seal on this world!"

862
01:46:37,670 --> 01:46:39,080
"I will write my name on it!"

863
01:46:42,670 --> 01:46:44,220
They said I wasn't ready.

864
01:46:46,180 --> 01:46:47,490
They said I was too young.

865
01:46:49,210 --> 01:46:50,590
They were right.

866
01:46:53,880 --> 01:46:55,590
But those who call it madness...

867
01:46:56,810 --> 01:46:58,060
... don't know that...

868
01:46:59,120 --> 01:47:01,850
... the charm is in my blood!

869
01:47:04,320 --> 01:47:06,550
Osman didn't start running yet!

870
01:47:08,560 --> 01:47:10,070
I'm still walking!

871
01:47:11,190 --> 01:47:15,840
The time will come, Osman will
be up to speed...

872
01:47:18,310 --> 01:47:22,280
... men from all around the world...

873
01:47:24,220 --> 01:47:26,510
... will wait at my Tent's door.

874
01:47:31,790 --> 01:47:34,010
Sacrifices will be made...

875
01:47:35,250 --> 01:47:36,980
... everywhere my essence reaches!

876
01:47:40,310 --> 01:47:42,280
How magnificent!

877
01:47:49,100 --> 01:47:50,200
Karayel!

878
01:47:50,440 --> 01:47:51,360
What is it?

879
01:47:51,890 --> 01:47:53,400
Did you get excited too?

880
01:47:53,830 --> 01:47:55,000
Come here you!

881
01:47:57,020 --> 01:47:58,890
We'll watch their tricks.

882
01:47:59,590 --> 01:48:00,720
We'll see them!

883
01:48:02,440 --> 01:48:04,180
We'll tame ourselves.

884
01:48:06,530 --> 01:48:08,920
We'll see who is friend, and who is enemy.

885
01:48:10,340 --> 01:48:14,940
Before we declare the strangers as
enemies, we'll purify ourselves.

886
01:48:15,850 --> 01:48:17,580
We'll clean our hearts!

887
01:48:21,680 --> 01:48:22,750
We'll bring justice...

888
01:48:23,430 --> 01:48:26,860
... to everywhere we step on!

889
01:48:28,550 --> 01:48:30,520
We'll walk a straight path...

890
01:48:31,030 --> 01:48:32,980
... without going out of Allah's way.

891
01:48:33,820 --> 01:48:36,520
We'll take our beloved Bala...

892
01:48:37,090 --> 01:48:39,320
... and turn our Tent into a
garden of roses.

893
01:48:54,910 --> 01:48:57,670
You shall be my witness, Karayel.

894
01:48:59,960 --> 01:49:01,330
I swear...

895
01:49:02,930 --> 01:49:07,180
... I'll destroy the tricks of those
who try to trick us!

896
01:49:08,360 --> 01:49:09,740
I'll bring justice...

897
01:49:10,270 --> 01:49:13,510
... to the whole world by
dignifying the truth.

898
01:49:14,620 --> 01:49:19,860
I won't bow to anyone but my Rab!

899
01:49:20,520 --> 01:49:22,990
I will be the ancestor of the valiants...

900
01:49:23,310 --> 01:49:25,070
... who happily sacrifice themselves!

901
01:49:49,320 --> 01:49:50,930
Selamın Aleyküm
(Peace be unto you)

902
01:49:51,710 --> 01:49:53,290
Ve Aleyküm Selam
(Peace be unto you too)

903
01:49:54,130 --> 01:49:55,850
May I come in, Sheikh Edebali?

904
01:49:56,630 --> 01:49:57,950
Come in, Alişar Bey.

905
01:50:29,340 --> 01:50:32,440
As you preserved it, it must be precious.

906
01:50:40,370 --> 01:50:41,850
This is from...

907
01:50:42,870 --> 01:50:47,020
our commander hz Ahmed Yesevi.

908
01:50:50,800 --> 01:50:53,100
The mother of pearl protects himself.

909
01:50:55,280 --> 01:50:57,010
So do volume of the book.

910
01:50:58,700 --> 01:51:00,900
Do you have something to say, Alişar
Bey?

911
01:51:02,150 --> 01:51:03,670
Yes, Sheik Edebalı.

912
01:51:05,000 --> 01:51:06,820
I say, we unite our power.

913
01:51:08,840 --> 01:51:12,120
We produce, we sell.

914
01:51:13,280 --> 01:51:15,300
I have contacts...

915
01:51:15,700 --> 01:51:18,620
and you have the skills.

916
01:51:19,250 --> 01:51:20,380
What is your goal?

917
01:51:22,600 --> 01:51:25,590
If we unite, we succeed.

918
01:51:27,230 --> 01:51:29,530
And we can take over the trade
around here.

919
01:51:48,910 --> 01:51:52,210
It seems that this year will be arid.

920
01:51:52,710 --> 01:51:56,890
If it doesn't snow, we can't feed
the animals in summer.

921
01:51:58,130 --> 01:52:02,010
I suggest we go to Domaniç Mountains
and look for a upland, uncle.

922
01:52:04,010 --> 01:52:05,140
Eyvallah. (Thank you)

923
01:52:07,120 --> 01:52:08,180
However...

924
01:52:09,250 --> 01:52:12,540
Alişar doesn't allow our mobility.

925
01:52:13,450 --> 01:52:15,850
He is afraid of us.

926
01:52:16,330 --> 01:52:17,700
He does.

927
01:52:18,400 --> 01:52:21,090
He does, but, he wants Aygül, uncle.

928
01:52:23,070 --> 01:52:25,180
He needs your friendship.

929
01:52:26,550 --> 01:52:30,830
My biggest regret is about my
daughter Aygül.

930
01:52:32,330 --> 01:52:33,900
I won't give my daughter to him.

931
01:52:41,400 --> 01:52:44,860
Alişar Bey, you know our past.

932
01:52:46,060 --> 01:52:49,080
Infidels will not leave us alone.

933
01:52:49,330 --> 01:52:51,910
Don't worry about what happened recently.

934
01:52:52,530 --> 01:52:54,990
I can protect us.

935
01:52:56,430 --> 01:52:59,320
If necessary, I can send an army to the
bazaar.

936
01:53:00,320 --> 01:53:03,290
I just need you to accept our partnership.

937
01:53:04,240 --> 01:53:06,130
Only our Lord...

938
01:53:07,130 --> 01:53:10,330
can give without taking something,
Alişar Bey.

939
01:53:10,570 --> 01:53:14,200
What do you want in return?

940
01:53:15,150 --> 01:53:16,860
Strong alliances...

941
01:53:17,340 --> 01:53:21,270
involve family, and then...

942
01:53:21,880 --> 01:53:23,950
the relatives, my Sheik.

943
01:53:29,970 --> 01:53:31,430
For this reason...

944
01:53:33,820 --> 01:53:38,180
In the name of Allah and witnessing of
our prophet...

945
01:53:39,210 --> 01:53:42,840
I want your daughter Bala in marriage.

946
01:53:49,430 --> 01:53:52,710
My Aygül is a delicate flower.

947
01:53:53,420 --> 01:53:57,160
I worry that she may fade in this
politics fight.

948
01:53:59,730 --> 01:54:01,340
You shouldn't...

949
01:54:02,130 --> 01:54:04,940
give your daughter to someone like
Alişar, uncle.

950
01:54:08,500 --> 01:54:10,160
That's what I think.

951
01:54:11,460 --> 01:54:12,810
That's what I think too.

952
01:54:14,660 --> 01:54:17,670
However, I gave my word...

953
01:54:18,490 --> 01:54:21,360
I promised...

954
01:54:22,100 --> 01:54:25,290
there is only one way to break
this promise.

955
01:54:27,200 --> 01:54:30,620
For Kayı's goodness and our tent's
safety...

956
01:54:32,270 --> 01:54:35,860
I want to give my daughter Aygül to you.

957
01:55:05,470 --> 01:55:08,870
I don't plume myself, but this is really
pretty.

958
01:55:10,180 --> 01:55:12,910
I will prepare these for your marriage,
my Aygül.

959
01:55:17,530 --> 01:55:19,130
There is something wrong with you.

960
01:55:20,210 --> 01:55:21,730
Tell me.

961
01:55:22,400 --> 01:55:23,810
My father...

962
01:55:24,090 --> 01:55:25,790
he doesn't trust Alişar Bey.

963
01:55:27,830 --> 01:55:32,120
He doesn't want this marriage because
he thinks we will be unhappy.

964
01:55:33,350 --> 01:55:35,120
Isn't that good news, my Aygül?

965
01:55:36,270 --> 01:55:40,030
I know you are not in love with that man.

966
01:55:41,550 --> 01:55:43,350
What can I do, Burçin?

967
01:55:44,650 --> 01:55:45,720
Tell me.

968
01:55:46,490 --> 01:55:49,070
Why did Osman step back?

969
01:55:49,690 --> 01:55:50,940
Why did he give up?

970
01:55:53,780 --> 01:55:56,110
She won't give up on Bala Hatun.

971
01:55:57,570 --> 01:55:59,170
Sooner or later...

972
01:56:00,580 --> 01:56:03,130
He'll bring her to the tent.

973
01:56:03,840 --> 01:56:05,940
He'll marry her.

974
01:56:08,700 --> 01:56:10,410
What will Aygül do?

975
01:56:12,200 --> 01:56:15,920
Osman and Bala will be here
and they'll be lovers.

976
01:56:23,490 --> 01:56:26,230
I'll distribute spindles on their wedding.

977
01:56:30,150 --> 01:56:32,520
Then when they have kids...

978
01:56:33,230 --> 01:56:35,090
I'll distribute cranberry sherbet.

979
01:56:36,360 --> 01:56:37,470
No...

980
01:56:38,560 --> 01:56:40,830
I can't stand it.

981
01:56:41,330 --> 01:56:43,660
It kills me slowly every day.

982
01:56:48,730 --> 01:56:51,050
I won't give up even if my father does.

983
01:56:52,180 --> 01:56:54,650
I'll marry Alişar Bey.

984
01:56:56,430 --> 01:56:58,090
I'll be the wife of...

985
01:56:58,570 --> 01:57:00,260
... the Banner Lord.

986
01:57:02,710 --> 01:57:05,120
I'll be happy to help my tent.

987
01:57:05,720 --> 01:57:07,930
I don't care about other things.

988
01:57:09,850 --> 01:57:12,340
It doesn't matter who it is...

989
01:57:14,250 --> 01:57:16,110
... as long as he's not the one I want.

990
01:57:17,380 --> 01:57:18,890
It's destiny, my Aygül.

991
01:57:22,260 --> 01:57:23,810
It's destiny, Burçin.

992
01:57:26,410 --> 01:57:28,030
But if I stay...

993
01:57:28,840 --> 01:57:31,690
... my destiny will be nothing
but suffering...

994
01:57:52,910 --> 01:57:55,070
Alps! Let's rest a little bit.

995
01:58:56,270 --> 01:58:58,250
Protect Gündüz Bey!

996
01:59:02,680 --> 01:59:04,100
Gündüz bey!

997
01:59:14,160 --> 01:59:15,450
Gündüz Bey!

998
01:59:20,570 --> 01:59:21,440
My Bey!

999
01:59:26,670 --> 01:59:28,160
Gündüz Bey!

1000
01:59:38,140 --> 01:59:42,140
"I bear witness that there is no
deity but Allah and...

1001
01:59:43,210 --> 01:59:46,600
... I bear witness that Muhammad
is the messenger of God."

1002
02:00:15,530 --> 02:00:16,540
My Bey!

1003
02:00:26,060 --> 02:00:26,880
My Bey!

1004
02:00:30,330 --> 02:00:31,430
My Bey.

1005
02:00:50,640 --> 02:00:52,790
May I come in, Selcan Hatun?

1006
02:00:54,890 --> 02:00:56,950
Come in, Zöhre Hatun.

1007
02:01:12,290 --> 02:01:15,620
Hatuns made this. They
shared it with people.

1008
02:01:16,360 --> 02:01:19,370
That's yours. Enjoy while eating.

1009
02:01:20,110 --> 02:01:23,550
Thanks. And
may Allah bless their hands.

1010
02:01:28,420 --> 02:01:30,430
There's something else.

1011
02:01:31,640 --> 02:01:34,630
You have a problem. Tell me.

1012
02:01:38,800 --> 02:01:41,510
I have. I do.

1013
02:01:42,810 --> 02:01:45,110
But how can I tell you?

1014
02:01:45,490 --> 02:01:49,340
Just tell me.

1015
02:01:52,020 --> 02:01:53,360
Selcan Hatun.

1016
02:01:53,690 --> 02:01:57,020
You know, we affianced Aygül
and Alişar Bey.

1017
02:01:57,590 --> 02:01:59,240
Yes, I know.

1018
02:01:59,860 --> 02:02:02,450
As if we needed him so much.

1019
02:02:02,940 --> 02:02:05,140
Dündar Bey hesitates too.

1020
02:02:05,680 --> 02:02:07,620
He doesn't want to hurt Aygül.

1021
02:02:08,320 --> 02:02:12,040
But he made a promise and
he can't go back.

1022
02:02:12,050 --> 02:02:13,300
Promise?

1023
02:02:13,540 --> 02:02:16,510
It's a curse that you promised.

1024
02:02:17,080 --> 02:02:20,530
You can't trust this kind of people.

1025
02:02:20,830 --> 02:02:25,060
Yes, but he is a Banner lord.

1026
02:02:25,560 --> 02:02:30,290
If we don't let him marry Aygül, he'll
torture all of the tent.

1027
02:02:31,620 --> 02:02:33,210
It's a pity.

1028
02:02:33,480 --> 02:02:37,940
Zöhre, you have something in your mind.
Tell me.

1029
02:02:38,680 --> 02:02:42,060
Tell me so we can think about it.

1030
02:02:43,880 --> 02:02:45,390
I say...

1031
02:02:46,090 --> 02:02:49,630
Only Osman can save Aygül.

1032
02:02:50,260 --> 02:02:53,250
Selcan Hatun, help us.

1033
02:02:54,370 --> 02:02:57,440
Let's espouse Aygül and Osman.

1034
02:02:59,720 --> 02:03:03,990
And Osman won't suffer anymore
because of that desperate love.

1035
02:03:04,810 --> 02:03:07,230
And Aygül will be safe.

1036
02:03:08,160 --> 02:03:10,360
Only you can solve this.

1037
02:03:12,100 --> 02:03:16,560
The thing that you have in
mind will harm us, Zöhre.

1038
02:03:20,450 --> 02:03:22,950
Aygül is our one and only, of course.

1039
02:03:23,790 --> 02:03:27,790
But Osman is the backbone of this tent.

1040
02:03:29,230 --> 02:03:31,210
As to what you said...

1041
02:03:33,240 --> 02:03:35,790
It's too complicated.

1042
02:03:43,220 --> 02:03:46,730
So that we can protect our tent.

1043
02:03:47,920 --> 02:03:48,970
I know.

1044
02:03:49,660 --> 02:03:52,390
You love Bala Hatun but...

1045
02:03:52,790 --> 02:03:56,000
Edebali didn't allow it, Osman.

1046
02:03:56,520 --> 02:03:59,440
Don't ruin yourself anymore.

1047
02:04:05,220 --> 02:04:06,730
Talk, boy.

1048
02:04:08,280 --> 02:04:09,750
What do you think?

1049
02:04:11,550 --> 02:04:12,740
Uncle...

1050
02:04:16,180 --> 02:04:17,990
May I come in, my Bey?

1051
02:04:18,180 --> 02:04:19,820
Come in, Saltuk.

1052
02:04:24,180 --> 02:04:26,490
My Bey, Gündüz Bey...

1053
02:04:26,780 --> 02:04:28,470
He was ambushed.

1054
02:04:28,950 --> 02:04:32,010
- Where is he?
- In Ertuğrul Bey's tent.

1055
02:04:35,340 --> 02:04:36,820
My Gündüz!

1056
02:04:40,970 --> 02:04:42,730
Lay him down.

1057
02:04:42,790 --> 02:04:44,480
Hurry up!

1058
02:04:44,980 --> 02:04:48,000
Come on. Easy.

1059
02:04:51,690 --> 02:04:53,890
Bring cauters.

1060
02:04:56,920 --> 02:04:58,370
Gündüz...

1061
02:04:59,030 --> 02:05:01,180
We have to take the arrow out.

1062
02:05:13,290 --> 02:05:14,790
Brother...

1063
02:05:24,450 --> 02:05:25,600
Brother.

1064
02:05:25,890 --> 02:05:28,890
Gündüz. Who did this to you?

1065
02:05:29,300 --> 02:05:30,350
Who?

1066
02:05:40,440 --> 02:05:42,070
Brother.

1067
02:05:42,520 --> 02:05:45,660
I'll drown those people in your blood.

1068
02:05:50,420 --> 02:05:53,430
Brother...

1069
02:06:05,090 --> 02:06:07,000
Brother.

1070
02:06:14,140 --> 02:06:17,080
Brother! Brother!

1071
02:06:17,970 --> 02:06:20,640
Gündüz! No!

1072
02:06:23,660 --> 02:06:25,050
Aunt?

1073
02:06:36,230 --> 02:06:38,350
Brother.

1074
02:06:41,650 --> 02:06:47,350
Trade, production and bazaar are
important, Alişar Bey.

1075
02:06:48,500 --> 02:06:52,500
We do this for Muslims to
produce some things...

1076
02:06:52,710 --> 02:06:56,310
... so they won't need the infidels.

1077
02:06:56,810 --> 02:06:59,100
We have the same aim, my Sheikh.

1078
02:07:00,830 --> 02:07:03,670
That's why I want to collaborate.

1079
02:07:04,740 --> 02:07:07,460
If you let me...

1080
02:07:07,460 --> 02:07:11,110
I want your family to adorn
my mansion with tiles.

1081
02:07:16,140 --> 02:07:19,000
As to Bala...

1082
02:07:21,220 --> 02:07:27,420
Bala grew up with Islamic
monastery and laws.

1083
02:07:28,810 --> 02:07:31,910
Her talent is for Islamic monastery.

1084
02:07:33,850 --> 02:07:36,140
Not for Bey palaces.

1085
02:07:37,580 --> 02:07:41,570
You're the ruler of these lands.

1086
02:07:41,760 --> 02:07:44,080
Your tables are wide...

1087
02:07:44,190 --> 02:07:46,420
... pursuers are plenty...

1088
02:07:46,810 --> 02:07:48,870
... your burden is heavy.

1089
02:07:50,630 --> 02:07:52,820
Bala isn't your cup of tea.

1090
02:07:54,560 --> 02:07:58,110
And I don't allow it. Know that.

1091
02:08:21,720 --> 02:08:26,750
Your consent cuts what my
sword can't, my Sheikh.

1092
02:08:27,460 --> 02:08:30,030
As you wish.

1093
02:08:33,350 --> 02:08:37,230
But you should think about it.

1094
02:08:38,160 --> 02:08:40,840
My offer is always valid.

1095
02:08:50,250 --> 02:08:53,990
Being the groom of such a magnificent
man like you...

1096
02:08:53,990 --> 02:08:56,820
... is better than being the Banner Lord.

1097
02:08:58,070 --> 02:09:01,820
You should know that with a single word
of yours, my world changes...

1098
02:09:02,440 --> 02:09:04,870
... my darkness lightens up.

1099
02:09:08,740 --> 02:09:12,570
My Gündüz! Who did this to you?

1100
02:09:12,570 --> 02:09:16,520
My Allah! Please! My Gündüz!

1101
02:09:21,700 --> 02:09:24,310
Osman. Relax, brother.

1102
02:09:25,120 --> 02:09:28,800
Mother! Is my Gündüz Ağa alive?
Say something!

1103
02:09:46,510 --> 02:09:48,160
He's breathing!

1104
02:09:50,830 --> 02:09:54,600
Slowly, but he's still
breathing, thankfully!

1105
02:09:54,600 --> 02:09:55,950
Thankfully!

1106
02:09:59,230 --> 02:10:01,450
May my Rab give him back to us.

1107
02:10:02,560 --> 02:10:04,500
May Allah not burn our hearts.

1108
02:10:04,500 --> 02:10:09,880
My Allah! A magnificent man is going away.
I'm burning!

1109
02:10:10,290 --> 02:10:13,280
My Allah give him back to me!

1110
02:10:13,280 --> 02:10:16,400
Shhh. Patience, my daughter.
Patience, Ayşe.

1111
02:10:16,600 --> 02:10:19,920
Heat up some iron.
Aygül, the water is boiling.

1112
02:10:20,310 --> 02:10:23,580
Bring the rags, we need to take
the arrows out.

1113
02:10:24,670 --> 02:10:29,070
Aunt, tell me. Will my brother be okay?

1114
02:10:34,860 --> 02:10:37,470
Be prepared for everything, Osman.

1115
02:10:59,480 --> 02:11:06,020
Your Bey was shot right in front of you!
What were you doing, huh? Tell me!

1116
02:11:06,870 --> 02:11:09,910
Osman Bey, if it was a battle, we would
have died for our Bey.

1117
02:11:09,910 --> 02:11:12,260
Didn't you see their faces?
How many were they?

1118
02:11:12,260 --> 02:11:14,700
They were far away. Infidels shot him
and ran away.

1119
02:11:14,700 --> 02:11:17,210
They were gone before we
realised what was going on.

1120
02:11:18,640 --> 02:11:22,920
Zöhre, do the best of what's necessary.

1121
02:11:23,210 --> 02:11:26,540
Medicine, or doctors...

1122
02:11:26,540 --> 02:11:31,350
... I'll bring everything. As long as
my nephew recovers.

1123
02:11:33,970 --> 02:11:37,970
My brother wanted me
to take care of him.

1124
02:11:52,020 --> 02:11:57,200
Pull yourself together, my nephew!
It's time we use our senses.

1125
02:11:57,450 --> 02:12:00,560
- Relax.
- How can I relax, Uncle!

1126
02:12:00,560 --> 02:12:03,840
How can I relax while my brother
is fighting for his life?

1127
02:12:05,950 --> 02:12:08,470
Who is this jackal attacking our herd?

1128
02:12:08,900 --> 02:12:13,760
My nephew, if you're suspicious
of someone, tell me!

1129
02:12:29,470 --> 02:12:33,470
Here is the hardest part.
It's close to the heart.

1130
02:12:40,410 --> 02:12:43,960
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim
(in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

1131
02:13:02,360 --> 02:13:04,190
O The Healer!

1132
02:13:06,630 --> 02:13:08,610
He's losing a lot of blood, mother!

1133
02:13:09,580 --> 02:13:14,390
Gündüz. Gündüz I'd die for you, please
open your eyes.

1134
02:13:14,520 --> 02:13:20,470
He's breathing. Don't worry.
He's here, Ayşe Hatun. Relax a little.

1135
02:13:21,320 --> 02:13:24,240
Hold on, my Gündüz. Hold on my lion!

1136
02:13:25,360 --> 02:13:28,560
Thank you, my Allah. Help us!

1137
02:13:28,560 --> 02:13:32,890
Thankfully, my Gündüz is still with us.
My Allah gave him back to us!

1138
02:13:36,620 --> 02:13:39,170
Aunt, it will be okay, right?

1139
02:13:39,170 --> 02:13:45,070
The only cure for these scars,
is to pray, Ayşe Hatun. Pray.

1140
02:13:47,090 --> 02:13:50,480
Aygül, we need to sear the scar.

1141
02:13:52,550 --> 02:13:54,870
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim
(in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

1142
02:13:55,950 --> 02:13:59,100
Whoever the enemy is,
they will come to light.

1143
02:13:59,100 --> 02:14:03,300
Before that, no one leaves the Tent alone.
Batur!

1144
02:14:03,690 --> 02:14:07,090
Increase the number of guards! Increase
the frequency of night watches.

1145
02:14:07,480 --> 02:14:11,370
War is near! We need to be alert.

1146
02:14:11,950 --> 02:14:15,800
- As you wish, father.
- The Alps! Go!

1147
02:14:20,300 --> 02:14:24,630
Ask around for any witnesses.

1148
02:14:24,630 --> 02:14:29,960
I say it was the castle, father.
Only the infidels do such an ambush.

1149
02:14:31,370 --> 02:14:33,990
If it was the castle, there
would be no survivors.

1150
02:14:35,030 --> 02:14:40,070
Whoever it is, they are threatening us.
The arrows were not shot at my brother.

1151
02:14:41,370 --> 02:14:44,680
They were shot at the Tent,
at our hearts!

1152
02:14:48,450 --> 02:14:53,920
If it wasn't the castle, then only Alişar
is brave enough to do this!

1153
02:14:55,030 --> 02:14:58,810
- Why would alişar do something like this?
- I don't know the reason.

1154
02:14:58,810 --> 02:15:03,630
But, who else is brave enough to do this?

1155
02:15:05,110 --> 02:15:12,370
Osman, my nephew. If there's
something you know...

1156
02:15:12,370 --> 02:15:13,620
... tell us.

1157
02:15:13,860 --> 02:15:18,190
I'm wondering just like you, uncle. Order
me, and I shall look for traces.

1158
02:15:22,110 --> 02:15:25,000
Come on now. Come on!

1159
02:15:28,850 --> 02:15:32,850
Brothers, be quick, come on!
Osman Bey will be out any second.

1160
02:15:33,080 --> 02:15:35,810
- We'll look for traces.
- Wait now, brother.

1161
02:15:36,080 --> 02:15:37,920
We don't know what's going on yet.

1162
02:15:38,530 --> 02:15:41,380
My Boran. Don't you know Osman Bey?

1163
02:15:41,380 --> 02:15:45,140
He'll come out through that door, and say
"We'll look for traces!"

1164
02:15:45,140 --> 02:15:48,470
In his heart, he has fire which
can burn the whole world!

1165
02:15:48,970 --> 02:15:50,260
Thank you, brother.

1166
02:15:50,260 --> 02:15:54,140
If we don't turn this world into hell for
those who did this...

1167
02:15:54,140 --> 02:15:56,070
... our reputation will be gone.

1168
02:16:03,880 --> 02:16:06,560
Osman Bey, how is Gündüz Bey doing?

1169
02:16:07,200 --> 02:16:11,070
- He'll be okay if Allah permits.
- If Allah permits, my Bey.

1170
02:16:12,890 --> 02:16:16,510
My Bey! Tell us and we'll melt mountains!

1171
02:16:18,430 --> 02:16:22,430
Alişar learned what we did.
He wants us to pay for it.

1172
02:16:23,900 --> 02:16:30,090
He'll see our power! He'll see how we turn
this world into hell for traitors!

1173
02:16:30,090 --> 02:16:36,370
My Osman! Who does something like this?
Who tried to kill my Gündüz?

1174
02:16:36,370 --> 02:16:38,860
That dog Alişar who eats from
the enemy's food.

1175
02:16:39,270 --> 02:16:41,070
That dog Alişar?

1176
02:16:41,700 --> 02:16:46,760
So it's time to take our swords and go to
battle, yell and find traces?

1177
02:16:47,260 --> 02:16:53,110
My sides have been aching for a while,
I've been dreaming of battle for a while.

1178
02:16:53,290 --> 02:16:55,180
Thank you, my Rab!

1179
02:16:55,850 --> 02:16:57,590
We'll ambush them.

1180
02:16:58,280 --> 02:17:01,910
We'll show them who is
the master of the battle.

1181
02:17:02,020 --> 02:17:04,690
Come on then, my Osman.
Come on my lions, to the horses!

1182
02:17:04,690 --> 02:17:08,060
Bamsı Bey! You should stay in the tent.

1183
02:17:08,850 --> 02:17:11,690
We need eyes to see, ears to hear.

1184
02:17:13,410 --> 02:17:15,390
You know my place.

1185
02:17:17,030 --> 02:17:19,790
Thank you, Osman. You're right.

1186
02:17:20,450 --> 02:17:23,140
I know your place, thank you.

1187
02:17:23,700 --> 02:17:25,370
Alps!

1188
02:17:26,360 --> 02:17:31,060
Come on, valiants! Come on lions! Come on!

1189
02:17:33,220 --> 02:17:34,860
How magnificent!

1190
02:17:34,860 --> 02:18:49,190
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com